From d1d89b87a07ffa90d1d0bb1e78d52ea18f4134da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:04:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native metadata, schema verification and
 legacy-artifact refusal

Port io/metadata.rs and the open-time checks of chronik-indexer's
indexer.rs to the native core:

- MetadataReader/Writer over the meta table: SCHEMA_VERSION (postcard
  u64), TOKEN_INDEX_ENABLED, LOKAD_ID_INDEX_ENABLED and
  SCRIPTHASH_INDEX_ENABLED (postcard bool), byte-compatible with Rust;
- schema version semantics of verify_schema_version: a newer DB is
  "Chronik outdated", an older one requires -chronikreindex, a missing
  version on a non-empty DB and an undecodable one are errors, and an
  empty DB is stamped with version 13, all with the Rust error texts;
- the index flag rules: disabling the token or LOKAD-ID index clears its
  tables, enabling the token index on a non-empty DB is an error, and
  enabling the LOKAD-ID or scripthash index on a non-empty DB asks the
  caller to reindex it;
- refusal of a directory holding legacy RocksDB files, with the Rust
  guidance text;
- refusal of a DB built with Rust Chronik plugins (non-empty plugin_meta),
  which the native implementation cannot keep in sync. Unlike Rust, the
  refusal happens before any flag is rewritten, so the DB is untouched;
- NATIVE_LAST_WRITER, a diagnostic postcard String naming the native
  implementation, written on every open (Rust reads only the keys it
  knows).

Tier: eCash
---
